{"status":"completed","summary":"node1 now runs a rootless nginx web container as the unprivileged, non-login account appsvc. It serves HTTP on port 8080 and recovered automatically after a verified node reboot without an interactive appsvc login session.","actions_performed":["Installed Podman and rootless-container dependencies.","Created appsvc with UID 1000, a nologin shell, and subordinate UID/GID ranges.","Enabled systemd lingering for appsvc.","Created a Podman Quadlet user service with restart policy and boot activation.","Published TCP port 8080 and added a persistent firewalld rule.","Rebooted node1 exactly once and verified recovery under a changed boot identity."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Application runs rootlessly as unprivileged appsvc","command_ids":["cmd-1e33ff309e4d4947","cmd-8f27d185ab904913","cmd-9f49b86257c840e1"],"summary":"appsvc is UID 1000 with subordinate IDs and a nologin shell. Podman reports the webapp container running, while host process output shows its container master process owned by appsvc."},{"requirement":"Web application serves on port 8080","command_ids":["cmd-bd48924d87d84b40","cmd-8f27d185ab904913","cmd-b0fb4a31f853412d"],"summary":"The persistent firewall rule is present, 0.0.0.0:8080 is listening, and requests to node1's managed IP returned HTTP 200 with the nginx welcome page before and after reboot."},{"requirement":"Service starts at boot without an active appsvc login session","command_ids":["cmd-8f27d185ab904913","cmd-b0fb4a31f853412d","cmd-9f49b86257c840e1"],"summary":"The generated user service is active with lingering enabled after reboot. appsvc's only session is Class=manager/Service=systemd-user with no TTY and Remote=no; its login shell is nologin."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-8f27d185ab904913","cmd-5d5fe1c5c7f64f9b","cmd-26cda608d8dc468d","cmd-b0fb4a31f853412d"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 2c237d4f-82f7-45c7-a304-4536d3b717e8 was captured, the safe reboot was acknowledged, the new boot ID 0a24ac8a-794a-48ae-a4f7-84fe01f05509 proved restart, and post-reboot checks confirmed the user service, container, listener, firewall, and HTTP response recovered."}]}
